From: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 05:45:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: drain flows when the last block unbinds

Disabling hardware offload unbinds the flow blocks, and netfilter sends
no destroy transaction for the rules it had installed. Their rows stay
valid in hardware and keep claiming the traffic they were built for,
which black-holes the wired hosts they point at until the next boot.

Drain the remaining rules once the last block is gone, reusing the
teardown path that already exists for module removal.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.18/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
Signed-off-by: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_flowtable.c
@@ -3536,6 +3536,13 @@ int ppe_flowtable_setup_tc(struct net_de
 			flow_block_cb_remove(block_cb, f);
 			list_del(&block_cb->driver_list);
 		}
+
+		/* Netfilter sends no destroy transaction for the rules it
+		 * installed here, so their rows would keep owning traffic
+		 * in hardware once the last block is gone.
+		 */
+		if (list_empty(&ft->block_cb_list))
+			ppe_ft_flow_drain(ft);
 		return 0;
 	default:
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
